    <!-- 0 WELCOME -->
    <section class="screen active">
      <span class="tag">Mini-Lesson</span>
      <h1>Spoken Language Endorsement</h1>
      <p class="big">This mini-lesson trains the <b>skills</b> the Edexcel Spoken Language Endorsement tests: preparing and giving a clear <b>formal presentation</b>, using <b>Standard English</b>, and <b>listening and responding</b> to questions from your audience.</p>
      <figure>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 560 150" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Three parts of the spoken language task">
          <rect x="12" y="35" width="170" height="82" rx="14" fill="#d9ebff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="97" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#0b5bbf">Present</text>
          <text x="97" y="90" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="12" fill="#0b5bbf">a prepared talk</text>
          <rect x="196" y="35" width="170" height="82" rx="14" fill="#efe1ff" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="281" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#6a30b8">Respond</text>
          <text x="281" y="90" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="12" fill="#6a30b8">to questions</text>
          <rect x="380" y="35" width="170" height="82" rx="14" fill="#d6f6e4" stroke="#2c2840" stroke-width="3"/>
          <text x="465" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Fredoka" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="#137a45">Standard English</text>
          <text x="465" y="90" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="12" fill="#137a45">clear &amp; formal</text>
          <text x="280" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Nunito" font-size="12.5" fill="#6b6580">Graded Pass / Merit / Distinction — reported separately</text>
        </svg>
      </figure>
      <p>Work through each screen, answer the <b>questions</b> as you go and collect ⭐ stars. Press <b>Start</b> when you're ready.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 1 WHAT IT IS -->
    <section class="screen">
      <span class="tag lo">Know the endorsement</span>
      <h2>What the endorsement is (and isn't)</h2>
      <p>The Spoken Language Endorsement is <b>teacher-assessed and internally set</b>. You give a <b>formal presentation</b> to an audience, then <b>answer questions</b> on it. It is:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Graded separately</b> — Pass, Merit or Distinction.</li>
        <li><b>Not part of your GCSE grade</b> — it does <b>not</b> count towards your 9–1 English Language result, but it appears on your certificate.</li>
        <li><b>Assessing</b> <span class="hl k">AO7</span> (demonstrate presentation skills in a formal setting), <span class="hl el">AO8</span> (listen and respond appropriately to spoken language, including to questions and feedback) and <span class="hl c">AO9</span> (use spoken Standard English effectively in speeches and presentations).</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>Separate but not pointless.</b> Universities and employers see it, and it builds the real-world skill of speaking confidently to an audience.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2 Q: grading MCQ -->
    <section class="screen">
      <span class="tag">Quick check</span>
      <h2>How is it graded?</h2>
      <div class="activity">
        <div class="qline"><span class="qnum">?</span><span>How is the Spoken Language Endorsement reported?</span></div>
        <div class="opts" data-q="q1" data-why="The endorsement is reported separately as Pass, Merit, Distinction (or Not Classified). It does not contribute to the 9–1 English Language grade, but it does appear on the certificate.">
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">As part of your 9–1 English Language grade <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="1">Separately, as Pass / Merit / Distinction <span class="mk">✅</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">As a percentage added to Paper 1 <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
          <button class="opt" data-correct="0">It is not recorded anywhere <span class="mk">❌</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="feedback" id="fb-q1"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3 PLANNING THE TALK -->
    <section class="screen">
      <span class="tag lo">Preparation skill</span>
      <h2>Planning a strong presentation</h2>
      <p>A great talk is built before you speak. Plan for your <b>purpose</b> and <b>audience</b>:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Choose a topic you care about</b> — genuine interest shows and carries the audience.</li>
        <li><b>Have a clear line of argument</b> — one main idea, developed logically.</li>
        <li><b>Structure it</b> — a hook, three or four clear points, a strong close.</li>
        <li><b>Use cue cards, not a script</b> — headings prompt you without you reading aloud word-for-word.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note"><b>PAP</b> — Purpose, Audience, Point. Know why you're speaking, who to, and what your single main message is.</p>
    </section>

