    <!-- 5 Q: structure MCQ -->
    <section class="screen">
      <span class="tag">Quick check</span>
      <h2>Signposting</h2>
      <div class="activity">
        <div class="qline"><span class="qnum">?</span><span>Why do phrases like "Firstly…", "On the other hand…" and "To sum up…" matter more in a <b>talk</b> than in an essay?</span></div>
        <div class="opts" data-q="q2" data-why="Listeners can't re-read a speech, so verbal signposts guide them through your structure in real time, keeping them oriented. In an essay the reader can look back; in a talk they can't.">
